# Kernel reference

The DI kernel this product runs on. This is the pointer; the authoritative,
generated reference lives in the ultrastack module (`references/kernel.md`) and
in `go doc` — check there before recalling an API.

- Registration: `di.Provide(Ctor)`, `di.Module("name", ...)`, `di.Export[T]()`,
  `di.Bind[I](Ctor)`. `go doc github.com/bronystylecrazy/ultrastack/di Provide`.
- Parameters declare semantics: bare `T` (exactly one), `di.Many[T]` (all,
  empty OK), `di.Optional[T]` (`.Or(fallback)`), `di.Lazy[T]` (store, `.Get(ctx)`
  in a method — breaks cycles), `di.Runner` (`run.Go`/`run.Supervise`).
- Lifecycle by convention: implement `Start`/`Stop`/`Healthy(ctx) error` and the
  container finds them. `di.Supply` values are not managed.
- Per-operation state → scopes (`di.Scope[S]`, `di.Scoped`); runtime-keyed
  families → `di.PerKey`/`di.Family`. Read the framework reference for these.

The covenant: if `stack.Validate(Modules()...)` returns nil, the app boots. Keep
`TestWiring` and run it after every wiring change.
